      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-h/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) This factors as (3r −1)(r −3) = 0. [M1] The two roots are 1/3 and 3. The latter has |r| &gt; 1, so the infinite sum diverges: Convergence requires r = 1/3. [A1] Then u1 = 6/(1/3)3 , [A1] = 162 and the infinite sum is 162/(1 −1/3) = 243 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
